# Prettier ignore list
#
# autofix.ci runs `npx prettier --write .` on every pull request. This file
# keeps the formatter away from anything that is generated, content-hashed,
# or not code, so a formatting pass can never change a hashed asset name or
# desync the tree from `npm run build` (the deploy workflow verifies the
# generated *.html/*.js/*.css/*.xml/*.txt files with `git diff --exit-code`).

# --- Dependencies and build output ---
node_modules/
build/
dist/
.vite/
.wrangler/
.cache/

# --- Generated site output ---
# Regenerated by `npm run build` and verified by `git diff --exit-code`.
*.html
*.xml
robots.txt
llms.txt
llms-full.txt
_headers
_redirects
index-*.css
index-*.js
legal-*.css
legal-*.js
store-*.css
store-*.js
item-*.css
item-*.js
inquiry-*.css
inquiry-*.js
reel-download-*.js
package-lock.json

# --- Sources whose bytes name their output (content-hashed bundles) ---
# These build scripts hash their output filename from the source bytes, so
# reformatting the source changes the hash, the filename, and every reference
# to it -- breaking the deploy's generated-output check. Leave them stable:
#   - store-src/ and legal-src/ hash the RAW file bytes (store-<hash>.css).
#   - src/**/*.css is minified by esbuild/vite, and esbuild's CSS minifier is
#     formatting-sensitive: reformatting src/inquiry/inquiry.css changes the
#     minified bytes and therefore the content hash. (esbuild's *JS* minifier
#     is formatting-independent, so src/**/*.ts and src/**/*.js are safe.)
#   - home-src/ generates index.html, whose inline whitespace is non-deterministic
#     across builds and changes when build.mjs is reformatted.
store-src/
legal-src/
src/**/*.css
home-src/

# --- CI configuration ---
# Keep workflow YAML out of the formatter's reach.
.github/

# --- Media and editorial content (not code) ---
*.md
*.avif
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.webp
*.gif
*.svg
*.wav
*.mp3
*.aif
*.aiff
*.ogg
*.opus
*.flac
*.woff
*.woff2
fonts/
images/
audio/
reel/
